.* QUIRDBDIR: WRKRDBDIRE, the relational database directory's entries
.* with their options. Option 5's detail shows in the report viewer.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=RDBCL BASETYPE='CHAR 18'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=LOCCL BASETYPE='CHAR 24'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TEXTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 24'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=POSTO CLASS=RDBCL.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=RDB CLASS=RDBCL.
:VAR NAME=RMTLOC CLASS=LOCCL.
:VAR NAME=RDBTEXT CLASS=TEXTCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=RDBS VARS='OPT RDB RMTLOC RDBTEXT'.
:KEYL NAME=KEYS HELP=KEYSHLP.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F6 ACTION='RETURN 6'.F6=Print list
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F22 ACTION='RETURN 22'.F22=Display entire field
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKRDBDIRE KEYL=KEYS HELP=WRKRDBH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SPACE.Work with Relational Database Directory Entries
:DATA DEPTH=2.
:DATACOL WIDTH=24.
:DATACOL WIDTH=78.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/POSTO' VAR=POSTO USAGE=INOUT.Position to
:EDATA.
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=RDBS SCROLL=YES MAXHEAD=2.(No entries)
:LISTACT HELP='WRKRDBDIRE/OPTIONS' OPTION=1 ENTER='CMD ?ADDRDBDIRE'.1=Add
:LISTACT HELP='WRKRDBDIRE/OPTIONS' OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD ?CHGRDBDIRE RDB(&RDB.)'.2=Change
:LISTACT HELP='WRKRDBDIRE/OPTIONS' OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD RMVRDBDIRE RDB(&RDB.)'.4=Remove
:LISTACT HELP='WRKRDBDIRE/OPTIONS' OPTION=5 ENTER='RETURN 105'.5=Display details
:LISTACT HELP='WRKRDBDIRE/OPTIONS' OPTION=6 ENTER='RETURN 106'.6=Print details
:LISTCOL HELP='WRKRDBDIRE/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Option
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/RDB' VAR=RDB USAGE=OUTPUT.Entry
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/RMTLOC' VAR=RMTLOC USAGE=OUTPUT.Remote Location
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/RDBTEXT' VAR=RDBTEXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Text
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKRDBH.Work with Relational Database Directory Entries - Help
:P.The databases this system knows by name: the local one and the
remote ones DRDA and DDM reach, each with where it is.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=KEYSHLP.Function keys - Help
:P.F3 and F12 leave, F5 reads the directory again.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='FLD/POSTO'.Position to
:P.Type the position to.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKRDBDIRE/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RDB'.Entry
:P.The entry of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RMTLOC'.Remote Location
:P.The remote location name of the system at the other end of the
connection.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RDBTEXT'.Text
:P.The text of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKRDBDIRE/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Add
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to add it. The Add RDB
Directory Entry (ADDRDBDIRE) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change RDB
Directory Entry (CHGRDBDIRE) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.4=Remove
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to remove it. The Remove RDB
Directory Entry (RMVRDBDIRE) command runs for the entry.
:PT.5=Display details
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display details it.
:PT.6=Print details
:PD.Type 6 next to an entry and press Enter to print details it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
